# DRONE ESCORT. A drone that follows a diver on its own, keeps out of the rock, and lets its coilgun shoot monsters
# but never the diver. Tested in sandbox/world/drone_escort.sbx (the Drone Range).
#
# What the game gives a drone to work with (reference/VEHICLE_MECHANICS.md):
#  * nothing reports where a character is; a motion detector only says "someone is inside my box". So the diver is
#    found by four big boxes around the drone (right, left, above, below, each set to Target=Human and
#    MinimumVelocity=0, which makes them presence detectors). The gap between the boxes is where the drone waits.
#  * rock is found by four small boxes (Target=Wall) just outside the hull, which only see rock while moving;
#  * the coilgun's AutoOperate (with AllowAutoOperateWithWiring set in the sub editor) already aims at the nearest
#    monster, never targets its own crew, and holds fire while a friendly diver is first in the line of fire. The
#    circuit only switches it on while a monster box (Target=Monster) sees something; that wire doesn't pass this box.
name drone_escort
box follow
note "DRONE ESCORT: HOW IT WORKS" "Wanted speed across = 2.5 m/s toward the side box that sees the diver (right minus left), up or down 1.5 m/s the same way. Nothing seen on an axis (the diver is close, or lost) = hold still on that axis.\nEngine and ballast = 60 x (wanted - actual speed), so the drone stops instead of drifting past.\nRock: heading into a wall box that sees rock stops that axis; blocked across, it climbs (or sinks, if there's rock above) to get around, for 1 s after the rock goes out of sight.\nStatus: FOLLOW, or DETOUR while going around rock."
note "WIRING" "in1 <- nav current_velocity_x, in2 <- nav current_velocity_y\nin3 <- diver box right, in4 <- diver box left, in5 <- diver box above, in6 <- diver box below (motion detectors, Target=Human)\nin7 <- wall box right, in8 <- wall box left, in9 <- wall box above, in0 <- wall box below (Target=Wall)\nout1 -> nav velocity_in, out2 -> status display\nOutside the box: monster box (Target=Monster, big) state_out -> coilgun set_auto_operate."
# measured speed in m/s (the nav terminal says km/h; y positive = sinking)
c kms mem Value=0.2778
c vx mul
c vy mul
w in1 vx.1
w in2 vy.1
w kms.out vx.2 vy.2
# wanted speed toward the diver
c hx sub
c hy sub
w in3 hx.1
w in4 hx.2
w in6 hy.1
w in5 hy.2
c k25 mem Value=2.5
c k15 mem Value=1.5
c tvx mul
c tvy mul
w hx.out tvx.1
w k25.out tvx.2
w hy.out tvy.1
w k15.out tvy.2
# rock in the way: stop that axis; blocked across = go around vertically
c bR and
c bL and
c bD and
c bU and
w in3 bR.1
w in7 bR.2
w in4 bL.1
w in8 bL.2
w in6 bD.1
w in0 bD.2
w in5 bU.1
w in9 bU.2
c bX or TimeFrame=1
c bY or TimeFrame=0.5
w bR.out bX.1
w bL.out bX.2
w bD.out bY.1
w bU.out bY.2
c zero mem Value=0
c xm mux
w bX.out xm.set_input
w tvx.out xm.signal_in0
w zero.out xm.signal_in1
c up mem Value=-1.2
c down mem Value=1.2
c dd mux
w in9 dd.set_input
w up.out dd.signal_in0
w down.out dd.signal_in1
c ym1 mux
w bX.out ym1.set_input
w tvy.out ym1.signal_in0
w dd.out ym1.signal_in1
c ym mux
w bY.out ym.set_input
w ym1.out ym.signal_in0
w zero.out ym.signal_in1
# engine and ballast from the speed error
c evx sub
c evy sub
w xm.out evx.1
w vx.out evx.2
w ym.out evy.1
w vy.out evy.2
c kv mem Value=60
c cx mul ClampMin=-100 ClampMax=100
c cy mul ClampMin=-100 ClampMax=100
w evx.out cx.1
w evy.out cy.1
w kv.out cx.2 cy.2
c cat concat Separator=,
w cx.out cat.1
w cy.out cat.2
w cat.out out1
# status
c sF mem Value=FOLLOW
c sD mem Value=DETOUR
c sm mux
w bX.out sm.set_input
w sF.out sm.signal_in0
w sD.out sm.signal_in1
w sm.out out2
